From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 06:10:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: s6e3ha9: Add brightness control

The panel does not take DCS brightness: Samsung sets the level with the
AOR duty together with the ELVSS and VINT levels, latched by a gamma
update. Register a backlight device that programs those three from the
vendor tables.

The tables are transcribed from the vendor panel description
(LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_exynos9820, commit 7d08ec364a06,
drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/panel/s6e3ha9/s6e3ha9_beyond2_a3_s0_panel.h
for AOR, ELVSS and VINT, and the matching _panel_dimming.h for the
brightness and luminance steps), taking the room temperature slice.

What this does not do is compute the per level gamma curve from the
panel's MTP data, which is the other half of what the vendor calls AID
dimming: the panel keeps the gamma programmed at power on, so a given
step will not hit its nominal luminance exactly. The 16 high brightness
mode levels above 255 are left out as well.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3ha9.c | 194 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 176 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3ha9.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3ha9.c
index b0683f5e534..ccc83368108 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3ha9.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-s6e3ha9.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
